# Calibration M (protocol step2-v1). Indices follow CALIBRATION_KEYS.json order.
1 IA m=M | MAP.md responsibility split assigns instruction content to owners (rules/CLAUDE.md, workflow skills, knowledge skills, hooks); it governs where instructions live and how pointers relate, not product code or the agent's output.
2 CO WF-010 m=MN d=WF | WF-010 "independent read-only review"; disallowedTools Write/Edit/NotebookEdit is the mechanism of the same read-only duty (C3). Bash remains available, so the tool restriction is narrower than the duty; no extra obligation.
  e: Bash is not in disallowedTools (read-only for Bash rests on the instruction text, code-reviewer.md:18)
3 CD DEP-003 m=MN k=W st=S | check-manifests.mjs:231-232 pushes a violation for any '*', bracket or comma version with no explicit-request branch; DEP-003 permits floating versions "unless explicitly requested". Remainder: the checker reports a violation (returned as a blocking reason by the dependency hook) even for an explicitly requested floating/range version, and also for every NuGet bracket form incl. exact [1.2.3] pins.
  x: Floating/range versions are always checker violations, with no explicit-request exception (NuGet '*', '[', '(' or ',' incl. exact bracket pins; npm empty/*/x/latest/next/>=)
  s: User explicitly asks for "8.*" of a package: DEP-003 allows it; the M checker still reports a violation the agent is told to address.
  fhd: Whether the explicit-request exception of DEP-003 should also be honoured by the manifest checker (checker vs skill text tension, Step-1 APPARENT_CONFLICT with FG-M-9c1350e27f).
  t: check-manifests.mjs over csproj, Directory.Packages.props, package.json (run by dependency-guard/file-change hooks and verify)
4 CD DEP-020 m=D k=W c=M | DEP-020 makes Microsoft resilience the default and direct Polly "an explicit exception rather than the default". add-dependency SKILL.md:27-30 narrows the admissible reason ("only when a concrete requirement cannot be expressed through those packages") and adds a documentation duty ("document why"). C7: the oracle DEFAULT does not itself require documenting the deviation.
  x: Direct Polly only when the Microsoft packages cannot express the concrete requirement, and the reason must be documented
  s: Agent adds Polly directly because an adjacent service already uses it, without writing the reason down: permissible as a reasoned DEFAULT deviation under DEP-020, not under the M skill.
5 XP m=D c=M rel=DEP-023,RUN-009,WF-007 | Directory.Build.props:11 sets AnalysisLevel=latest for every project imported from the root; this is executable build configuration (selects the analyzer rule set, so diagnostics change) and no policy requires a particular analysis level; DEP-023 only fixes where shared settings live. Projects may override (MSBuild), hence DEFAULT. Effect is diagnostic (warnings) unless warnings are escalated elsewhere.
  s: A repository keeping the SDK default analysis level satisfies all 196 policies; M's shared props make every project build with the latest analyzer rule set, surfacing additional CA diagnostics.
6 CO PST-010 PST-008~ m=M d=WF c=M | First part restates PST-010 (treat migrations as source, review before committing, same attention list). "Review DbSeeder together with" a migration changing seeded entities is a procedural part of PST-008 (update the seeder in the same change when seeded entities are affected), which requires examining the seeder; it adds no behavior PST-008 does not already force, but covers PST-008 only partly (review, not the update duty).
7 NN fa=FC c=M rel=DEP-003,DEP-025 | Facet states how hook-io.mjs postToolBlock behaves for PostToolUseFailure: the reason is passed as additionalContext instead of decision:block. It narrows the enforcement channel of the target group FG-M-89479fb15b for failed commands and adds no obligation; static reading only (C10), host semantics of PostToolUseFailure not executed.
8 IA m=D | project-structure SKILL.md:23-24 tells the workflow which private reference files to read per task ("not all of them by default"): instruction loading/routing inside the instruction system, no product or work-output behavior; outside oracle scope.
